# CLAUDE.md

This project builds all UI with the **General Design System (GDS)** — `@doneisbetter/gds`. Follow `AGENTS.md` (same directory) for the full rules. Summary:

- **Provider:** the app is wrapped once in `GdsProvider`. Never add a second provider.
- **Compose, don't reinvent:** import shipped components from `'@doneisbetter/gds'`. No raw Mantine primitives, no ad-hoc HTML/CSS controls where a GDS contract exists.
- **Style via props + tokens:** `c`, `bg`, `mt`, `p`, `variant`, `color`, `size`, `radius`, and GDS layout primitives. No custom CSS classes, no raw hex/px in feature code.
- **Actions:** `SemanticButton action="save|add|edit|delete|…"` (semantic enum). Selects take `data={[{value,label}]}`.
- **States:** design loading / empty / error / disabled / success (`StateBlock`, `EmptyState`).
- **Access:** gate private/paid content with `GdsAccessGate protectedContentPolicy="never-render-while-locked"`.
- **Accessibility & responsive/localized layout** are acceptance criteria, not cleanup.

Before building new UI, check `COMPONENTS_AND_PATTERNS.md` and the API reference for an existing contract. Read a component's `<Name>Props` type and compose it — the shipped component already encodes correct behavior, accessibility, and responsive intent.

